# .clinerules — Pipeline Constitution for MIGRATE
# Mirrors AGENTS.md rules. Included for compatibility with automated checkpoint scripts.
# The authoritative source is AGENTS.md; this file must never contradict it.

## Identity
This project is the MIGRATE Legacy Python Equivalence Converter.
Agents: Om (Classifier), Suryansh (Converter+Critic), Pritam (Verifier), Agent D (CLI Orchestrator).

## Must Always
- Always run in a sandbox before reporting success.
- Always treat the sandbox diff as the authoritative behavioral signal.
- Always surface every function in the report (build/summary.json).
- Always preserve a critic concern — needs_review survives even on clean sandbox.
- Always keep needs-review visible without blocking merges.

## Must Never
- Never silently mark an ambiguous or failed result as passing.
- Never send a conversion_failed function to the verifier.
- Never call the LLM for a function that isn't classified llm_needed.
- Never call the converter/critic for a function classified unsupported.
- Never let a single function's conversion_failed halt the batch.
- Never let internal CI pass/fail counts gate the internal build.
- Never redefine shared/schemas.py unilaterally to route around a teammate's output shape.
